<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices quiet, undertone steady.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices quiet, undertone steady.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were quiet with new arrivals at around 10,000 tonnes in central Indian markets on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were down by 200 rupees per tonne on increased supply from plants and refineries. The undertone was easy and business volume was thin.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were strong on better export demand against tight supply. Soymeal yellow was quoted at $265 per tonne and rapeseed extraction fetched $127.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was quoted at 4,300 rupees FOR Bedibunder and at 4,250-4,275 FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
